e to be characterized using currently-available\nparameters can be simulated by writing supplementary Python code that\ncharacterizes the reform.","position":{"start":{"line":31,"column":1},"end":{"line":31,"column":1}},"key":"TWAMzjfQEt"}],"key":"x48QmaH1xV"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":38,"column":1},"end":{"line":41,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Tax-Calculator can estimate for each filing unit the marginal tax rate\ngenerated by a small change in income.  Marginal tax rates can be\ngenerated for nineteen different kinds of income.  And marginal tax\nrates can be estimated under any parametric tax reform.","position":{"start":{"line":38,"column":1},"end":{"line":38,"column":1}},"key":"EYu5ntIl2W"}],"key":"VyAxy0wP5Z"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":43,"column":1},"end":{"line":49,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Tax-Calculator is extensively tested using hundreds of unit and\nintegration tests that achieve complete code coverage.  Also, there is\nan ongoing cross-model validation effort that uses large\nrandomly-generated samples of filing units to compare results\ngenerated by Tax-Calculator with results from other tax models.  The\ncross-model validation work is described\n","position":{"start":{"line":43,"column":1},"end":{"line":43,"column":1}},"key":"c6o2u85Uow"},{"type":"link","url":"https://github.com/PSLmodels/Tax-Calculator/blob/master/taxcalc/validation/README.md","position":{"start":{"line":43,"column":1},"end":{"line":43,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"here","position":{"start":{"line":43,"column":1},"end":{"line":43,"column":1}},"key":"ES2irXpFb1"}],"urlSource":"https://github.com/PSLmodels/Tax-Calculator/blob/master/taxcalc/validation/README.md","data":{"kind":"file","org":"PSLmodels","repo":"Tax-Calculator","reference":"master","file":"taxcalc/validation/README.md","raw":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PSLmodels/Tax-Calculator/master/taxcalc/validation/README